cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use diffractom, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "diffractom: GPU-accelerated texture tomography of scanning diffraction data"
version: 0.2.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Carøe"
    given-names: "Martin Sæbye"
    affiliation: "Technical University of Denmark"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/msaca-okse/diffractom"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.20431766
    description: "Concept DOI on Zenodo: all versions of diffractom (resolves to the latest)"
abstract: >-
  diffractom is a GPU-accelerated (OpenCL) Python library for texture tomography of scanning
  diffraction data, in particular scanning three-dimensional X-ray diffraction (s3DXRD). From
  azimuthally integrated ring intensities, indexed by rotation angle, translation, azimuth and ring,
  it reconstructs the orientation distribution function of every pixel in a sample slice, expanded
  in Gaussian kernels on an orientation grid. The forward operator combines a pole-figure transform
  with a parallel-beam Radon transform, and FISTA solves for non-negative coefficients.
keywords:
  - texture tomography
  - s3DXRD
  - scanning 3DXRD
  - X-ray diffraction
  - orientation distribution function
  - OpenCL
  - GPU
